.TH CSTRING_COPY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_copy \- create an independent copy of a string
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr cstring_copy(cstr s, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function allocates a new cstring with the same content as s. After
the call the two strings are fully independent of each other.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     String to copy
err   Optional pointer to receive an error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new cstring on success
NULL when an allocation fails; the details then go to *err when err is
not NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
You must destroy the returned cstring once you are done with it
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_substring (3),
.BR cstring_create (3)
